    solution_walkthrough: "**Identify the problem type** Recoil / 'explosion' problem - one body separating into two in an isolated system.\n\n**Governing principle** Conservation of Momentum. With no external forces, total momentum stays at its initial value of zero.\n\n**Assumptions** Deep space (no gravity or drag), astronaut and wrench form an isolated system, spacecraft interaction ignored.\n\n**Execute** Initial momentum is zero, so final must be zero:\n$$0 = m_a v_a + m_w v_w$$\n$$v_a = -\\frac{m_w v_w}{m_a} = -\\frac{(5)(12)}{80} = -0.75\\,\\text{m/s}$$\n\n**Answer** $0.75\\,\\text{m/s}$ in the direction opposite the thrown wrench.\n\n**Sanity check** She is $16\\times$ more massive than the wrench, so her speed should be $16\\times$ smaller: $12/16=0.75$ - matches.\n\n**How an interviewer probes this** 'Was kinetic energy conserved?' No - the chemical/muscular energy of the throw created KE from a zero-KE start; momentum is conserved, energy is not.",
