    time_limit_seconds: null,
    parts_json: null,
    tier: "difficult",
    solution_walkthrough: "**Identify the problem type** Multi-body related rates: two moving ships, a midpoint, and a fixed elevated observer (3-D distance).\n\n**Governing principle** Related rates via implicit differentiation of a 3-D distance built from a constant-speed midpoint.\n\n**Assumptions** Straight constant-velocity paths from a common origin; drone fixed at altitude $12$ km over the port; flat Earth.\n\n**Execute** Positions: A$=(15t,0)$, B$=(0,20t)$. Midpoint $M=(7.5t,10t)$. Ground distance from port:\n$$s=\\sqrt{(7.5t)^2+(10t)^2}=12.5t,\\quad \\frac{ds}{dt}=12.5.$$\nDrone-to-midpoint distance: $D=\\sqrt{s^2+12^2}$, so $D\\frac{dD}{dt}=s\\frac{ds}{dt}$. At $t=2$: $s=25$, $D=\\sqrt{625+144}=\\sqrt{769}\\approx27.73$.\n$$\\frac{dD}{dt}=\\frac{25(12.5)}{\\sqrt{769}}\\approx11.27\\text{ km/h}.$$\n\n**Answer** $\\frac{dD}{dt}\\approx11.3$ km/h (increasing).\n\n**Sanity check** As $t\\to\\infty$ the altitude becomes negligible and $dD/dt\\to12.5=ds/dt$; our value is slightly below that: consistent.\n\n**How an interviewer probes this** Likely: how does the answer change if the drone were above the midpoint instead of the port?",
