    solution_outline: "Split off one $\\sin$: $\\sin^2=1-\\cos^2$, let $u=\\cos x$, $du=-\\sin x\\,dx$. $\\int -(1-u^2)u^2du=\\frac{\\cos^5x}{5}-\\frac{\\cos^3x}{3}+C$.",
