    created_at: "2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z",
    time_limit_seconds: null,
    parts_json: null,
    tier: "intermediate",
    solution_walkthrough: "**Identify the problem type** A single-variable max/min (box volume) optimization.\n\n**Governing principle** Set the first derivative of the volume to zero.\n\n**Assumptions** Cuts are perfect squares; material has negligible thickness.\n\n**Execute** After folding, the base is $(30-2x)$ on a side and the height is $x$, so\n$$V(x)=x(30-2x)^2.$$\nDifferentiate (product/chain rule):\n$$V'(x)=(30-2x)^2 + x\\cdot 2(30-2x)(-2)=(30-2x)(30-6x).$$\nSetting $V'=0$: $x=15$ (degenerate, $V=0$) or $x=5$.\n\n**Answer** $x=5\\text{ cm}$, giving $V=5(20)^2=2000\\text{ cm}^3$.\n\n**Sanity check** $x$ must lie in $(0,15)$; $x=5$ is interior and $V(0)=V(15)=0$, so it is the max.\n\n**How an interviewer probes this** Expect: \"How would the answer change for a rectangular sheet, say $30\\times 40$?\"",
