    prompt_text: "An open-top rectangular tank with a square base must hold $32\\text{ m}^3$ of water. Find the base side length $s$ and height $h$ that minimize the total material (base plus four walls, no top).",
    first_principle_target: "Setting the first derivative to zero to locate an extremum",
    solution_outline: "Minimize $S=s^2+4sh$ with $h=32/s^2$, so $S=s^2+128/s$. $S'=2s-128/s^2=0\\Rightarrow s^3=64\\Rightarrow s=4\\text{ m}$, $h=2\\text{ m}$. Min material $=48\\text{ m}^2$.",
    major_category: "all",
