    created_at: "2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z",
    time_limit_seconds: null,
    parts_json: null,
    tier: "intermediate",
    solution_walkthrough: "**Identify the problem type** Constrained minimal-surface-area (open box) optimization.\n\n**Governing principle** Minimize surface area subject to fixed volume; set the derivative to zero.\n\n**Assumptions** Negligible wall thickness; square base; no top surface.\n\n**Execute** Volume constraint: $s^2 h=32\\Rightarrow h=\\dfrac{32}{s^2}$. Material (base + 4 sides):\n$$S=s^2+4sh=s^2+\\frac{128}{s}.$$\nDifferentiate: $S'(s)=2s-\\dfrac{128}{s^2}=0\\Rightarrow s^3=64\\Rightarrow s=4\\text{ m}$. Then $h=32/16=2\\text{ m}$.\n\n**Answer** $s=4\\text{ m}$, $h=2\\text{ m}$, minimum material $=16+128/4=48\\text{ m}^2$.\n\n**Sanity check** $S''=2+256/s^3>0$, a minimum; note $s=2h$, the expected proportion for an open square tank.\n\n**How an interviewer probes this** Likely: \"Redo it with a closed top; why does the optimal $s/h$ ratio change?\"",
